        /// <summary>
        /// Remove Vendor User ### Overview  Removes a user from your vendor account. The user must be owned by your vendor account. The user&#39;s TorBox account is not deleted, it is only released from the vendor, even though the &#x60;detail&#x60; of the response reads \&quot;User deleted successfully.\&quot;  What happens to the user&#39;s plan depends on the plan they are on when they are removed:  - If the user is on the same plan as your vendor account, the user is moved to the free plan (plan 0) and their &#x60;premium_expires_at&#x60; is set to the current time. - If the user is on a different plan than your vendor account, their plan and their &#x60;premium_expires_at&#x60; are left as they are.  Your vendor account&#39;s &#x60;current_users&#x60; is lowered by one, and the user receives a notification that they were removed from the vendor.  ### Rate Limits  This endpoint is rate limited to **1 request per second** per API token.  ### Authorization  Requires an API key using the Authorization Bearer Header. Works with an API key from any plan, including the free plan. 
